  "$comment": "M02e look pass (DL-704): the procedural look of the streamed city as data. Design values tuned in the M02e session (a config edit, not code, changes them). Colours are sRGB hex strings; the materials convert them to linear. The profile per tier: full on the desktop tiers, lite on mobile, min on mobile-low, legacy (the M02b1/M02b2 materials) on both XR tiers. M02g1 adds: bloom; grade (display-referred lift/gamma/gain, saturation and a warm-sun/cool-shade split, per weather preset, blended with the weather blend); haze (sun in-scatter, Rayleigh tint and extinction per kilometre, per preset); windows.litFrac (rows of [hour, min, max], cyclic and smooth: the share of a lit building's windows that are lit); layers (the layer ids each profile enables, legacy none); dynamicCasterRadiusM. M02h8 (DL-740): both XR tiers map to the xr profile (the min building path, flat paint, skyReflect, fog-node grade and haze, blobs, opaque crowns, vertex AO; no noise, bump, alpha test or post), legacy stays valid on every tier as the fallback; xr-visionpro has its shadow map off (shadowsOff: its csm1 map would draw twice, one per view pass) until M11b1's device run; postLevelCap 3 lets the governor put TRAA on desktop (level 3: gtao-half, bloom, traa, tonemap).",
